│                 │  └──────────────────────┘    │                 │
└─────────────────┴──────────────────────────────┴─────────────────┘
```

---

## 3. Left Sidebar

### 3.1 Board Selector
- Lists all boards with task count badges
- Active board: indigo left border + indigo name color
- "New Board" dashed button at bottom of list
- **New Board modal**: name + description fields

### 3.2 Column Filter Pills
- Pills: All | To Do | In Progress | Done | Blocked | [+ new col]
- "All" = show all task groups (default active)
- Selecting a specific column = filter task list to that column only
- Active pill: indigo border + indigo bg tint

### 3.3 Free-Text Search
**Searches across:** task name, assignee, data-search attributes (include file names, message excerpts, profiles in search tokens)

Behavior:
- Filters task rows in real time
- Hides entire column groups if all tasks are hidden
- Shows "No tasks found" empty state
- Clear (×) button appears when text is present

### 3.4 Task List (Grouped by Column)
Each column group contains:
- `slbl` section label with column color dot, name, count
- `+` button per group to add task in that column
- Task rows: status icon + name + hover "Sub" button

Task row states:
| State | Appearance |
|---|---|
| Default | `#9ca3af` name, transparent bg |
| Hover | `rgba(255,255,255,0.04)` bg |
| Selected | `rgba(99,102,241,0.12)` bg, white name |
| Done | strikethrough name |
| Blocked | red exclamation icon |

Clicking a task row → selects task (same as clicking the kanban card).

### 3.5 Sidebar Footer
- "New Task" button: indigo ghost style, full width
- "Collapse" button: collapses sidebar to width 0, exposes hamburger in topbar

---

## 4. Main Panel Top Bar

Contains (left → right):
1. Hamburger expand button (hidden when sidebar open)
2. View toggle: **Board** | **Chat** (pill style, active state)
3. Spacer
4. Task info (shown only when task selected): task name + column badge
5. Spacer
6. "+ Column" ghost button → opens New Column modal
7. "+ New Task" primary button → opens New Task modal
8. Task detail sidebar toggle button (icon only, shown when task selected)

---

## 5. Board View

Horizontally scrollable column layout. Each column:

### Column Header
- Color dot + column name + task count badge + `+` add-task button

### Task Cards
Minimum card content:
- Status icon (circle = todo, half = wip, check = done, exclamation = blocked)
- Task name (weight 500 if active/important, `#9ca3af` otherwise)
- Description snippet (11px muted, max 2 lines)
- **Mode badge**: Chat / Document / PR Review (indigo or red tint)
- Tags: subtask count, assignee, priority

Card states:
| State | Border | Background |
|---|---|---|
| Default | `#2e2e2e` | `#252525` |
| Hover | `rgba(99,102,241,0.35)` | `#2a2a2a` |
| Active/Selected | `rgba(99,102,241,0.6)` | `rgba(99,102,241,0.07)` |

Hover reveals "Sub" button (top-right of card) to add a subtask.

### Column Footer
Dashed "+ Add task" button, color matches column color on hover.

### New Column CTA
Dashed card at end of columns: `160px` wide, center-aligned icon + text.

---

## 6. Chat View (Primary Work Area)

The chat view is the **main work surface** — this is where the AI collaboration happens.

### Empty State (no task selected)
- Center-aligned icon + text + "New Task" button

### Task Workspace (task selected)
Layout (flex column, full height):
1. **Task header block** — sticky at top of message area:
   - Status icon + task name + column/assignee/mode metadata
   - Description text
   - File attachment chips (if any)

2. **Message thread** — scrollable:
   - User messages: right-aligned, indigo bg bubble
   - AI messages: left-aligned, dark bg bubble
   - Code blocks: dark monospace block inside AI bubble
   - Each message: avatar + author + time + bubble

3. **Input area** — fixed at bottom:
   - **Profiles bar**: chips showing assigned profiles (name + role + avatar initial)
   - Chat input textarea (Enter to send, Shift+Enter for newline)
   - Toolbar: paperclip, code mode, add-subtask, Send button

---

## 7. Task Modes

Each task has a **mode** that determines the AI context and icon:

| Mode | Icon | Color | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `chat` | `fa-message` | indigo | Open AI conversation, general work |
| `task` / Document | `fa-file-lines` | indigo | Document generation, structured output |
| `prview` / PR Review | `fa-code-pull-request` | red | Code review with AI inline comments |

Mode is set at task creation and shown as a badge on cards and in the detail panel.

---

## 8. Right Detail Panel

Slides in from right (300px). Toggle button in topbar.

### Sticky Header
- Status icon (colored bg) + task name + column badge
- Quick action buttons: Move | Subtask | Delete (danger)

### Scrollable Body Sections

**Description**
Dark `#242424` background box with full text.

**Meta Grid (2×2)**
- Priority (colored label)
- Mode badge
- Assignee
- Updated time

**Profiles** (like ChatSidebar `ProfileCard`)
Each profile chip: avatar initial (colored) + name + role

**Subtasks**
Each subtask: circle/check icon + name + column badge.
Done subtasks: strikethrough + gray name.
Empty state: text with inline "+ add one" link.

**Files**
Each file: code icon + filename + external link icon.

**Activity Log**
Chronological entries: colored icon badge + action text + relative time.
Separated by subtle horizontal rules.

