### New Board Modal
Fields:
- Board name
- Description

All modals:
- Centered, `backdrop-filter: blur(4px)`, dark overlay
- ESC key or clicking overlay = close
- Cancel + confirm buttons in footer

---

## 11. Color System

```
Primary:       #6366f1   (indigo – CTA, active states, chat mode)
Primary Light: #818cf8   (hover, secondary accent)

Todo:          #6366f1   (indigo)
In Progress:   #f59e0b   (amber)
Done:          #10b981   (emerald)
Blocked:       #ef4444   (red)

Surfaces:
  Main bg:     #111111
  Sidebar:     #1a1a1a
  Cards:       #252525
  Hover:       #2a2a2a
  Muted:       #242424

Text:
  Primary:     #e5e7eb
  Secondary:   #9ca3af
  Muted:       #6b7280
  Placeholder: #4b5563
```

---

## 12. Interactions & State Management

| Interaction | Result |
|---|---|
| Click task (sidebar or card) | Selects task, highlights both locations, switches to Chat view, opens detail panel, populates all panels |
| Click same task again | Deselects, hides detail, shows chat empty state |
| ESC key | Closes modals, or deselects task |
| "Board" view toggle | Shows horizontal kanban columns |
| "Chat" view toggle | Shows AI conversation workspace |
| Sidebar collapse | Width 0, reveals hamburger in topbar |
| Send message (Enter) | Appends user bubble, simulates AI "thinking" → response |
| Add Subtask | Opens task modal in subtask mode with parent pre-filled |
| Detail toggle btn | Slides right panel in/out |
| Column filter pill | Filters sidebar task list by column |
| Search input | Filters sidebar rows, hides empty groups, shows no-results state |

---

## 13. Responsive Considerations

- **Desktop-first** (1200px+): All 3 panels visible
- **Compact (900–1200px)**: Auto-collapse right detail until toggled
- **Tablet (<900px)**: Collapse sidebar by default, board scrolls horizontally
- Touch targets: minimum 44px for all buttons

---

## 14. Key Design Decisions (Rationale)

1. **Flat subtasks** — Avoid deep nesting complexity; subtasks are independent workspaces
2. **Board + Chat toggle** — Board view for overview/planning, Chat view for actual work execution
3. **Profiles in chat input** — Mirrors `ChatSidebar.vue` pattern; makes AI context visible
4. **Task header in chat** — Keeps task context visible without leaving the work area
5. **Mode badges on cards** — Differentiates chat tasks from document/PR tasks visually
6. **Right detail panel** — Non-blocking metadata; slides in from right to avoid losing chat context
7. **Search scope** — Sidebar search targets name + assignee + file names + message content (encoded in `data-search`)
